SUSPECTED BUG: (placeholder span "-") Slurp has a named result err that a deferred closure
overwrites with fmt.Errorf("source: close: %w", cerr). The final expectation (plan S08,
not implemented yet) is: os.Open origins under "source: open: %w", the io.ReadAll set
(readall_call_site) under "source: read: %w", sentinel source.ErrEmpty, and the Close set
(close_in_deferred_closure) under "source: close: %w". Today a variable captured and
written by a closure is documented as Unresolved(memory) "load of escaping variable err"
(e2e dynamic/freevar_other_closure_store), so 5 such entries, one per return plus the
recover exit, and no origins is the honest interim result: nothing is silently dropped.
What is wrong today is the entry for the recover exit: its span and its path hop are
printed as "-" although the output contract says an Unresolved entry's span is its site.
